    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure factor for membership level in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`.\n\n**What changed** \u2014 `getMembershipLevel()` previously had the comment \"level 4 is reserved for tenure\" but was hard-capped at 3 with no tenure logic. I made level 4 actually reachable:\n\n- Added a fourth factor: `+1` when tenure (days from `registrationDate` to the current date) exceeds 365.\n- Raised the cap from 3 to 4.\n- Updated the Javadoc to document all four factors and the new-owner guarantee.\n\n**Why a new owner never exceeds level 3** \u2014 a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is set to the effective (today-ish) date in `BuildOwner`, so its tenure is zero, far below the 365-day threshold. The three pre-tenure factors (base 1 + email + no-namesakes) therefore top out at 3. The acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` \u2014 a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` 0 \u2014 confirms level 3, and the audit log line in the run shows `membershipLevel=3`.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
