        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe tenure factor is added in exactly the right unit. `getMembershipLevel()` is already the `@Transient` derived property that composes per-factor booleans (`hasEmail`, `unique`) each contributing `level++`, and the new `tenured` boolean follows that same shape precisely \u2014 compute a boolean, increment, then cap with `Math.min`. The cap bump from 3 to 4 and the Javadoc rewrite are coherent with the spec.\n\nTenure is derived from `registrationDate`, a field on `Owner`, so the logic belongs here alongside the other derived getters (`getAgeBand`, `getMembershipNumber`, etc.) rather than in a service. No duplication: there was no pre-existing \"tenure in days\" helper to reuse (`getAgeBand` uses `Period.between` for age, a different computation), and the new `ChronoUnit` import is the natural tool. The method stays a focused three-factor accumulator, not a catch-all. A maintainer of this file would find the addition natural."
